    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d466-a1">

                <pb facs="0554" n="474" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg474"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Mann to Mr.
                            Hill.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >House of Representatives</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Chicago,
                                Ill.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1901-05-31"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">May 31,
                    1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: Referring to your kind favor of the
                    22d instant relating to the case of William Frederick Versluis, who is held as a
                    prisoner of war by the British Government, permit me to request that you make
                    proper representations to endeavor to obtain the release of Mr. Versluis on
                    parole on the understanding that he will return to the United States. His
                    brothers here are willing to furnish the passage money for his return home, and
                    will do so at such time and in such manner as may be indicated by you or
                    required.</p>
                <p>May I specially request that an effort be made to obtain the release on parole of
                    Versluis?</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James R. Mann.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
